WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: ar

00:00:15.289 --> 00:00:19.031
What will happen to this file now?

00:00:19.055 --> 00:00:22.555
Tip of the Iceberg

00:00:29.625 --> 00:00:31.859
Tip of the Iceberg

00:00:33.596 --> 00:00:36.830
Tip of the Iceberg
Destroying Evidence

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.476
In front of the cameras,

00:00:39.851 --> 00:00:44.085
an Israeli bullet assassinates our colleague,
Shireen Abu Akleh,

00:00:44.453 --> 00:00:47.313
through which the occupation
sought to assassinate the image

00:00:47.453 --> 00:00:48.841
and kill the truth

00:00:49.247 --> 00:00:51.250
However, this crime

00:00:51.645 --> 00:00:54.313
managed to revive dozens of files

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:57.737
of journalists who were killed
on Palestinian land

00:00:58.096 --> 00:01:00.993
whose names and the moments
when assassinated

00:01:01.422 --> 00:01:03.070
remained sculpted in people's minds

00:01:03.375 --> 00:01:04.969
Despite that, their lawsuits

00:01:05.211 --> 00:01:07.750
are still pursuing unfound justice.

00:01:32.191 --> 00:01:33.930
Ready!

00:01:35.084 --> 00:01:37.818
Quickly!
CALL THE AMBULANCE!

00:01:38.138 --> 00:01:40.977
AMBULANCE!

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.344
AMBULANCE!
Come Here!

00:01:44.523 --> 00:01:46.412
Stay there!
Stay with her!

00:01:46.912 --> 00:01:48.795
These terrifying snaps

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:52.099
documented the assassination of our colleague,
Shireen Abu Akleh,

00:01:52.443 --> 00:01:53.227
before the whole world

00:01:54.061 --> 00:01:57.891
On 11 May 2022,

00:01:58.194 --> 00:02:01.264
here in Jenin, Shireen was martyred

00:02:01.453 --> 00:02:05.328
with a bullet from an Israeli soldier
that targeted her directly

00:02:05.453 --> 00:02:07.910
and our colleague, Ali Al-Samoudi,
was also shot

00:02:08.152 --> 00:02:11.666
while accompanying her
to accomplish a journalistic mission.

00:02:12.088 --> 00:02:13.734
There is no god but Allah!

00:02:13.877 --> 00:02:15.813
One year has passed
since the assassination,

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:19.265
and the Israeli occupation
is still vigorously trying

00:02:19.562 --> 00:02:22.257
to avoid responsibility and pay the price

00:02:28.039 --> 00:02:31.234
The FBI took over

00:02:31.458 --> 00:02:33.247
the investigation into Shireen's case,

00:02:33.316 --> 00:02:35.315
as she held American nationality.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:44.852
According to the information we got,
a team of the FBI

00:02:45.162 --> 00:02:48.225
investigated Shireen's case on the ground,
away from the media,

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:51.367
in cooperation with
the Palestinian Public Prosecutor's Office

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:56.223
American experts also analyzed
video and audio clips

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:58.340
of the assassination incident

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:04.305
In this investigation,
we managed to interview Steven Beck

00:03:04.461 --> 00:03:06.953
the investigator and expert
who previously cooperated

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:09.734
with the American
Bureau of Investigation FBI

00:03:09.938 --> 00:03:13.813
The man undertook
an in-depth audio analysis task

00:03:14.156 --> 00:03:17.227
of the widely spread video clips
on Shireen Abu Akleh's assassination

00:03:20.824 --> 00:03:23.859
I have analyzed tens of thousands
of fire-shooting clips,

00:03:24.359 --> 00:03:28.094
so I have a good idea of
what I'm looking for.

00:03:28.406 --> 00:03:30.117
First of all,

00:03:30.203 --> 00:03:33.258
you start watching the video and listening
to the audio simultaneously

00:03:38.477 --> 00:03:41.617
Anyone injured?

00:03:43.383 --> 00:03:46.883
Ambulance!

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.578
Mujahed!

00:03:51.813 --> 00:03:54.375
I've been shot!

00:03:54.898 --> 00:03:56.680
Shireen! Oh man!
Shireen!

00:03:56.797 --> 00:04:00.953
But you couldn't see
where the bullets were coming from

00:04:01.055 --> 00:04:03.398
You couldn't see anyone shooting

00:04:03.461 --> 00:04:06.961
At that point,
I had to depend on the audio,

00:04:06.984 --> 00:04:10.898
and something else that drew my attention
was the surrounding.

00:04:10.992 --> 00:04:13.656
So, I noticed that
there was a group of journalists

00:04:13.805 --> 00:04:17.484
who were walking down the street

00:04:17.789 --> 00:04:21.797
In that street,
there were walls and houses too

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:26.539
So that was restraining the bullets' course

00:04:26.781 --> 00:04:31.592
Therefore, the audio contained much additional
information that was unavailable in the video

00:04:38.498 --> 00:04:40.427
So when the shooting started

00:04:40.459 --> 00:04:43.787
and the bullet caused a shock,

00:04:43.818 --> 00:04:47.412
after that, the muzzle blasted

00:04:47.623 --> 00:04:51.498
There was a time difference

00:04:51.537 --> 00:04:53.623
From the time difference,
I could calculate

00:04:53.654 --> 00:04:57.209
and estimate how far the shooter was

00:04:57.396 --> 00:04:59.748
According to my calculations,

00:04:59.779 --> 00:05:00.943
the shooter was

00:05:01.037 --> 00:05:09.677
at a distance between 180 to 201 metres

00:05:09.748 --> 00:05:10.781
We also discovered

00:05:11.445 --> 00:05:15.195
that there was a group of
Israeli Defense soldiers

00:05:15.562 --> 00:05:20.033
around 200 metres
away from that intersection

00:05:20.252 --> 00:05:25.900
where the journalist and the person
recording with the cell phone were

00:05:27.318 --> 00:05:31.990
So, the sound signature
matches the distance

00:05:32.552 --> 00:05:37.501
And those bullets were directed
towards the journalist.

00:05:37.526 --> 00:05:43.098
So, I firmly believe that
this supports the fact that

00:05:43.559 --> 00:05:50.201
the shots came from
the Israeli Defence (IDF) soldiers

00:05:59.716 --> 00:06:02.442
Were they targeting the journalists?

00:06:02.747 --> 00:06:07.519
They were definitely
aiming at the journalists

00:06:11.157 --> 00:06:13.094
To London,
the capital of the United Kingdom

00:06:13.555 --> 00:06:17.219
We went to meet a person
who experienced Israel's policies

00:06:17.593 --> 00:06:21.736
and practices in the file
of targeting journalists

00:06:21.767 --> 00:06:24.967
Detective Chris Cobb-Smith,
a former British Officer

00:06:25.214 --> 00:06:29.471
He investigated the killing of journalists
by the Israeli occupation army

00:06:29.995 --> 00:06:33.481
and was informed of the details of colleague
Shireen Abu Akleh's assassination

00:06:35.659 --> 00:06:40.113
First and foremost, the shot
that hit Shireen was not a random fire

00:06:40.138 --> 00:06:44.488
Although those shots were inconsistent,
they were intentional

00:06:44.513 --> 00:06:48.124
Some of the shots hit the tree

00:06:48.149 --> 00:06:51.020
close to where she was standing

00:06:51.117 --> 00:06:53.438
Those were not random shots

00:06:53.463 --> 00:06:58.293
How do you view the outcome of the
Israeli handling of Shireen's case?

00:06:58.361 --> 00:07:03.530
Will they repeat the way they dealt
with the killing of other journalists

00:07:03.743 --> 00:07:06.473
in addition to destroying evidence
and escaping from accountability?

00:07:07.421 --> 00:07:12.256
Yes. In fact, there was a
complete explanation

00:07:12.281 --> 00:07:14.577
in the investigation and an
admission of responsibility

00:07:14.702 --> 00:07:19.458
by the Israeli army
and the Israeli authorities

00:07:20.467 --> 00:07:23.930
They started to provide excuses
directly after the incident

00:07:24.001 --> 00:07:27.798
If you look in detail
at the people's locations

00:07:27.829 --> 00:07:29.894
and military units;

00:07:29.964 --> 00:07:32.481
where the journalists were standing;

00:07:32.581 --> 00:07:36.605
the distances,
and the footage filmed at that time,

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:40.916
then one of them will be blamed
for that incident

00:07:41.085 --> 00:07:43.561
Once again,

00:07:44.069 --> 00:07:49.034
I'm not sure the person responsible
will be held accountable

00:07:53.647 --> 00:07:56.330
One of the most prominent cases
that Smith investigated

00:07:56.590 --> 00:08:01.095
was the case of British journalist
James Miller in 2003,

00:08:01.279 --> 00:08:03.144
who was shot by an Israeli soldier

00:08:03.187 --> 00:08:06.113
in the city of Rafah
in the southern Gaza Strip

00:08:06.312 --> 00:08:08.291
Smith's investigation

00:08:08.448 --> 00:08:12.961
was at the official request of the Miller family
and the institution he worked for

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:15.044
and with the British government's support

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:19.313
The investigation documents in
the Miller case, which we reviewed,

00:08:19.556 --> 00:08:21.547
revealed the extent of Israeli manipulation

00:08:21.929 --> 00:08:25.014
and reflected a systematic policy
of targeting journalists

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:26.787
and evading punishment

00:08:26.930 --> 00:08:30.133
Like other cases
in which journalists were targeted

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:33.466
However, what is striking
in the James Miller case,

00:08:33.501 --> 00:08:34.976
according to Detective Smith,

00:08:35.376 --> 00:08:37.520
is a mistake made by the Israeli army

00:08:37.963 --> 00:08:41.895
in one of the investigations documents
provided to the family and their lawyer

00:08:42.659 --> 00:08:46.861
The error revealed an aspect the Israeli
military was keen to hide in the case

00:08:47.972 --> 00:08:50.421
We know that the Israeli army
always deliberately

00:08:50.499 --> 00:08:52.748
conceals the names
of the soldiers or officers

00:08:53.086 --> 00:08:54.649
directly responsible

00:08:55.057 --> 00:08:57.947
for involvement in the killings
and assassinations of journalists

00:08:58.230 --> 00:09:01.419
In James Miller's case, it was noted
that the officer's name

00:09:01.444 --> 00:09:02.035
was leaked,

00:09:02.651 --> 00:09:04.113
maybe by mistake, as you mentioned

00:09:04.657 --> 00:09:08.934
A document published
by the Israeli authorities

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:11.895
obscures all the individuals involved

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:13.500
Still, there was

00:09:13.525 --> 00:09:16.232
one name that was not hidden;

00:09:16.435 --> 00:09:18.355
a lieutenant

00:09:18.433 --> 00:09:20.612
in the Israel Defense Forces

00:09:20.637 --> 00:09:23.425
- Officer?
- An Officer, that's correct

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:25.145
Do you think that showing the name

00:09:25.474 --> 00:09:26.381
was by mistake?

00:09:26.406 --> 00:09:30.288
I believe it was by mistake
because it had been concealed

00:09:30.454 --> 00:09:32.346
It has been deleted from the entire report

00:09:32.405 --> 00:09:34.716
Yet, it appeared in one line only;

00:09:34.916 --> 00:09:37.398
therefore, we know who that officer is

00:09:38.588 --> 00:09:41.879
This is the document where
the Israeli officer's name was shown

00:09:42.296 --> 00:09:46.954
while it has been referred to
in the other documents with the code H

00:09:48.504 --> 00:09:52.654
After revealing the name of the Israeli officer
in addition to the British government's pressure on the case,

00:09:52.827 --> 00:09:55.067
correspondence that we viewed revealed

00:09:55.102 --> 00:09:58.529
a settlement offer made
by the Israeli Ministry of Defense

00:09:58.748 --> 00:10:00.962
through the British Embassy in Tel Aviv

00:10:01.456 --> 00:10:04.173
in December 2005

00:10:04.226 --> 00:10:05.607
to close the file

00:10:07.365 --> 00:10:08.823
In 2008,

00:10:09.266 --> 00:10:12.365
a settlement was announced
under which Israel paid

00:10:12.660 --> 00:10:17.556
financial compensation for one million
and 750 thousand pounds sterling

00:10:17.886 --> 00:10:19.232
to the family of James Miller

00:10:19.396 --> 00:10:23.840
in exchange for closing the file of the trial
of any Israeli soldier in the case

00:10:24.345 --> 00:10:25.801
Without this political pressure

00:10:26.168 --> 00:10:27.913
from the British government,

00:10:28.364 --> 00:10:30.153
do you expect
things would not have reached

00:10:30.205 --> 00:10:32.381
compensation and this outcome?

00:10:33.617 --> 00:10:35.301
As you know,

00:10:35.362 --> 00:10:38.842
I do not doubt that the pressure
from the British government

00:10:38.991 --> 00:10:42.377
significantly impacted
the Israeli authorities' response

00:10:42.463 --> 00:10:46.021
So, when it comes to
local Palestinian journalists,

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:48.790
there is no such political pressure

00:10:49.207 --> 00:10:50.231
and hence rights are lost

00:10:50.466 --> 00:10:52.401
It would seem so,

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:53.810
unfortunately

00:10:55.162 --> 00:10:57.780
While the family of the
British journalist received

00:10:57.805 --> 00:11:00.536
financial compensation supported
by the British government,

00:11:00.839 --> 00:11:04.176
the cases of local Palestinian journalists
piled up

00:11:04.385 --> 00:11:06.856
without justice
or any attempt at compensation

00:11:07.420 --> 00:11:08.818
One of the most prominent

00:11:08.943 --> 00:11:11.486
is the case of Palestinian journalist
Fadel Shana,

00:11:11.851 --> 00:11:15.106
the British Agency
Reuters' Cameraman in Gaza

00:11:16.451 --> 00:11:17.706
In 2008,

00:11:18.153 --> 00:11:21.920
he was targeted directly
by an Israeli tank shell

00:11:22.371 --> 00:11:25.609
while doing his journalistic work
in the middle of the Gaza Strip

00:11:29.919 --> 00:11:32.315
Fifteen years have passed
since the incident,

00:11:32.741 --> 00:11:35.250
without any accountability
or legal condemnation,

00:11:35.866 --> 00:11:38.965
it seemed as if the file
on his assassination had been closed

00:11:39.052 --> 00:11:42.785
Reuters sent a British team

00:11:44.677 --> 00:11:48.275
to investigate this file with lawyers

00:11:50.389 --> 00:11:52.733
but to no avail

00:11:53.376 --> 00:11:58.009
It was useless as this team
did not fulfil its investigations

00:11:59.861 --> 00:12:04.935
They fulfilled their investigations in
Gaza Strip with us as a family, a team, a place

00:12:05.277 --> 00:12:06.788
They inspected the location

00:12:06.953 --> 00:12:10.822
But they firmly refused
to deal with the Israelis

00:12:11.281 --> 00:12:16.332
As a family, we are following
the course of the case,

00:12:17.131 --> 00:12:24.900
Reuters assures us that
they will follow up on the file

00:12:25.745 --> 00:12:28.210
when the conscience
of the soldier or officer

00:12:28.496 --> 00:12:32.463
who gave the order to kill Fadel, wakes up

00:12:33.106 --> 00:12:41.040
We are still waiting for the conscience
of the Israeli soldiers to confess to killing Fadel

00:12:41.164 --> 00:12:45.524
deliberately and targeting Fadel personally

00:12:48.315 --> 00:12:52.447
This place is a witness to the killing of journalist
Fadel Shana by an Israeli tank shell,

00:12:52.985 --> 00:12:57.013
which led to his death along with other
young men and children who were near him

00:12:58.220 --> 00:13:00.633
One of those
who witnessed these bloody moments

00:13:01.069 --> 00:13:03.213
is the photojournalist Muhammad Al-Baba

00:13:20.928 --> 00:13:24.207
We arrived here;
this was the last point we could reach

00:13:24.398 --> 00:13:26.577
because the Israeli tank was in that area

00:13:26.768 --> 00:13:28.921
So, therefore, we were unable
to reach the event area

00:13:28.973 --> 00:13:32.220
It means we did not get to the mosque
where the incident occurred

00:13:33.727 --> 00:13:36.916
So, he got out of his car
and set up his tripod

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:40.844
It was like Fadel
to pay attention to everything

00:13:40.913 --> 00:13:44.517
related to security or occupational safety

00:13:44.736 --> 00:13:47.713
He had a small press Jeep
with the word "PRESS" on it,

00:13:47.783 --> 00:13:50.388
and he was standing right next to it

00:13:50.866 --> 00:13:56.288
I remember standing 10 metres away from him
and seeing him in front of me

00:13:56.765 --> 00:14:00.193
We were filming straight
in that direction

00:14:00.818 --> 00:14:03.412
And I remember in those days
that these buildings did not yet exist

00:14:04.072 --> 00:14:08.796
It was an empty area, and that was the place
where the Israeli tank was positioned

00:14:09.595 --> 00:14:12.723
We started filming, and Fadel was there,
ready with his camera

00:14:13.296 --> 00:14:16.429
We were also there,
pointing our cameras in that direction

00:14:16.773 --> 00:14:20.419
It wasn't a long distance
to presume that the tank did not see us

00:14:20.497 --> 00:14:23.058
On the contrary,
the tank could see us clearly

00:14:23.266 --> 00:14:27.355
We wore special clothes like jackets etc

00:14:27.407 --> 00:14:30.089
We also wore helmets on our heads
that had "PRESS" written on them

00:14:30.350 --> 00:14:34.248
Thus, we were visible to the Israeli tank

00:14:34.482 --> 00:14:37.382
Suddenly, while we were filming,
heavy gunfire started

00:14:48.132 --> 00:14:51.231
They assassinated Fadel
They wanted him dead

00:14:58.272 --> 00:15:03.205
From a distance of 10 metres,
I took two pictures focusing on Fadel

00:15:03.440 --> 00:15:06.308
I stood by Fadel and found his blood spilt
and his neck severed

00:15:06.621 --> 00:15:10.325
And I started screaming Fadel, Fadel...

00:15:10.504 --> 00:15:12.431
Because this was
one of the harrowing scenes,

00:15:12.562 --> 00:15:18.007
to see my colleague soaked in blood
and slaughtered

00:15:18.256 --> 00:15:19.427
It was a painful scene

00:15:19.982 --> 00:15:22.420
I remember stopping filming,

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:26.944
My entire body was shaking,
and I started screaming,

00:15:27.343 --> 00:15:31.119
and I couldn't control my nerves
or camera anymore

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:35.208
The Israeli army announced

00:15:35.607 --> 00:15:37.576
shortly after the assassinations
of Fadel Shana,

00:15:37.906 --> 00:15:41.873
a clear and complete vindication of
the tank crew from the assassination charge

00:15:42.663 --> 00:15:44.600
The Israeli army lawyer said

00:15:44.878 --> 00:15:47.194
that it was not clear to the soldiers

00:15:47.290 --> 00:15:49.961
whether Fadel was carrying
a camera or a gun

00:15:50.212 --> 00:15:52.773
and that the jacket he was wearing

00:15:53.025 --> 00:15:57.782
was similar to the jackets worn by
Palestinian terrorists, as they claim

00:15:57.834 --> 00:16:02.029
The lawyer concluded that
the tank crew acted appropriately

00:16:02.054 --> 00:16:03.785
and they would not face

00:16:03.895 --> 00:16:05.979
any legal action accordingly

00:16:06.713 --> 00:16:10.775
This targeting is done
clearly and publicly,

00:16:11.296 --> 00:16:14.803
with crude and unacceptable justifications

00:16:15.376 --> 00:16:18.987
that can be refuted

00:16:19.942 --> 00:16:21.670
Sometimes they say

00:16:22.069 --> 00:16:25.472
the camera looked like an RPG;

00:16:25.958 --> 00:16:28.884
they were in the wrong place
at the wrong moment;

00:16:29.491 --> 00:16:34.088
it was an unintentional target,

00:16:34.973 --> 00:16:37.785
and another target
should have been targeted

00:16:38.324 --> 00:16:40.049
They always find excuses

00:16:41.195 --> 00:16:44.736
In this investigation,
we contacted Reuters News Agency,

00:16:45.031 --> 00:16:46.642
seeking to conduct an interview

00:16:46.963 --> 00:16:51.162
and inquire about the latest developments in
the case of its journalist, Fadel Shana

00:16:51.594 --> 00:16:53.798
Its officials refused to be interviewed

00:16:54.163 --> 00:16:56.168
and sent a written response,

00:16:56.776 --> 00:17:00.676
“Everyone who handled this situation has moved on…”

00:17:01.195 --> 00:17:03.920
In his message,
a spokesman for the agency expressed

00:17:04.294 --> 00:17:06.512
deep sorrow for Fadel's loss

00:17:06.686 --> 00:17:09.507
and emphasised protecting
the rights of journalists

00:17:09.629 --> 00:17:11.304
wherever they are in their coverage

00:17:11.816 --> 00:17:14.907
Reuters was in charge of all these matters

00:17:16.695 --> 00:17:19.941
and followed them up with specialists

00:17:20.427 --> 00:17:23.081
from institutions to protect journalists

00:17:23.732 --> 00:17:25.112
Institutions

00:17:27.248 --> 00:17:30.174
to follow up on the files
of the killing of journalists

00:17:30.842 --> 00:17:31.754
Still,

00:17:32.317 --> 00:17:33.975
Reuters

00:17:34.662 --> 00:17:39.349
did not inform us of anything

00:17:40.199 --> 00:17:42.478
because Palestinian journalists

00:17:43.225 --> 00:17:45.317
are numbers

00:17:46.922 --> 00:17:52.721
for international and universal
news agencies and channels

00:17:56.002 --> 00:17:57.053
They cannot fight,

00:17:57.653 --> 00:17:58.668
or they cannot

00:17:59.927 --> 00:18:04.042
give, or confront Israel

00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:09.337
because of existing and shared interests

00:18:11.238 --> 00:18:13.880
In the documents we looked at
in this investigation,

00:18:14.259 --> 00:18:17.436
it was remarkable that
the Israeli Military Advocate General

00:18:17.783 --> 00:18:19.389
used the term military activity

00:18:19.823 --> 00:18:21.761
to describe what the soldiers were doing

00:18:21.887 --> 00:18:24.317
when the journalists were targeted

00:18:24.682 --> 00:18:27.590
The Israeli occupation army
relied upon a pretext

00:18:27.928 --> 00:18:30.512
to justify targeting
journalists and civilians

00:18:30.929 --> 00:18:32.726
and exempting its officers and soldiers

00:18:33.065 --> 00:18:34.740
from any legal responsibility

00:18:35.278 --> 00:18:38.481
It considers that whoever is present in

00:18:39.622 --> 00:18:41.756
the location of combat operations,

00:18:41.948 --> 00:18:45.030
and this, of course,
is a very loose and broad term

00:18:45.386 --> 00:18:47.538
used limitlessly

00:18:48.450 --> 00:18:54.546
by being in these places
and being exposed to harm,

00:18:54.738 --> 00:18:56.013
whether by gunfire,

00:18:56.038 --> 00:19:00.644
rubber bullets, injured or killed

00:19:01.087 --> 00:19:02.626
They consider that the state

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:08.136
is exempt from any responsibility
towards this person

00:19:08.440 --> 00:19:12.462
because he is in an area
of a combative nature.

00:19:13.568 --> 00:19:15.495
The Palestinian journalist Moath Amarneh

00:19:16.129 --> 00:19:19.164
lost an eye by an Israeli sniper's bullet

00:19:19.572 --> 00:19:22.162
that hit him
while covering a peaceful sit-in

00:19:22.428 --> 00:19:26.664
against settler attacks in November 2019

00:19:27.307 --> 00:19:28.452
in Surif,

00:19:28.779 --> 00:19:30.733
north of Hebron, in the West Bank

00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:32.769
And I was standing here,

00:19:33.285 --> 00:19:35.613
visible to the army

00:19:36.285 --> 00:19:40.395
I was 100% visible

00:19:46.771 --> 00:19:48.184
The camera is with me

00:19:50.817 --> 00:19:53.006
Something hit me
I didn't know what it was

00:19:53.154 --> 00:19:55.271
I felt at that time

00:19:55.693 --> 00:19:56.747
that my head had taken off

00:19:56.911 --> 00:20:00.060
I started shouting, "I'm injured"

00:20:00.545 --> 00:20:02.817
Journalists came around

00:20:02.957 --> 00:20:04.318
and tried to give me first aid

00:20:04.879 --> 00:20:06.551
At this time, the army came upon us

00:20:06.723 --> 00:20:08.371
One of them was carrying a camera
and filming

00:20:08.575 --> 00:20:10.529
He came to document this injury

00:20:11.143 --> 00:20:12.268
Since that time,

00:20:12.623 --> 00:20:13.651
Amarneh has not succeeded

00:20:13.742 --> 00:20:15.901
in moving forward with any legal action

00:20:15.964 --> 00:20:17.261
against the occupation soldiers

00:20:17.433 --> 00:20:19.144
before the Israeli judiciary

00:20:19.980 --> 00:20:22.748
We went to file a lawsuit,

00:20:23.787 --> 00:20:26.495
but we stopped and did not continue

00:20:26.520 --> 00:20:34.381
because the police dealt with the matter,

00:20:36.254 --> 00:20:40.603
and their response was so negative

00:20:41.009 --> 00:20:43.943
that they did not even hear

00:20:44.417 --> 00:20:45.355
any statement from me

00:20:47.812 --> 00:20:54.068
Their response was that the injury was in

00:20:54.513 --> 00:20:57.654
a site of operations

00:20:57.950 --> 00:20:59.873
or a military area

00:21:00.217 --> 00:21:04.863
in a state of war,
and the casualties in these areas

00:21:05.331 --> 00:21:08.357
they do not deal with

00:21:10.649 --> 00:21:15.881
We tried more than once, but

00:21:16.663 --> 00:21:19.616
their handling of the issue stopped us

00:21:19.960 --> 00:21:24.057
Because what we will do

00:21:24.167 --> 00:21:27.029
at that time is what we call
"shaking water"

00:21:27.279 --> 00:21:29.849
Meaning that no soldier
would be held accountable

00:21:29.982 --> 00:21:34.621
and the case
would not be dealt with as required,

00:21:34.692 --> 00:21:36.254
so we did not continue

00:21:37.032 --> 00:21:40.180
Unfortunately, the IDF seems,

00:21:40.313 --> 00:21:41.725
in such situations,

00:21:42.006 --> 00:21:44.827
seems to feel that
they can get away with anything

00:21:44.960 --> 00:21:47.206
Not only the James Miller incident,

00:21:47.440 --> 00:21:49.456
which I thoroughly investigated

00:21:49.636 --> 00:21:52.348
and spent a lot of time working on

00:21:52.512 --> 00:21:55.848
I was involved in investigating

00:21:55.965 --> 00:21:58.622
Tom Hurndall's shooting
and Rachel Corey's death

00:21:59.059 --> 00:22:02.496
These incidents do not appear
to be taken seriously

00:22:02.886 --> 00:22:04.504
It also seems the soldiers are confident

00:22:04.575 --> 00:22:07.490
they can get away with it

00:22:07.754 --> 00:22:10.927
because whatever they do,
their actions will be covered up,

00:22:11.029 --> 00:22:12.200
which is unacceptable

00:22:12.458 --> 00:22:13.771
It is unacceptable

00:22:13.852 --> 00:22:15.434
that they claim to be

00:22:15.459 --> 00:22:18.928
one of the most powerful militaries
in the world

00:22:20.178 --> 00:22:24.646
Statistics indicate that 55 journalists
have been killed since 2000

00:22:24.998 --> 00:22:26.966
by Israeli occupation bullets

00:22:27.162 --> 00:22:30.895
in the West Bank and Gaza Strip

00:22:31.240 --> 00:22:32.406
Yasser Murtaja,

00:22:32.662 --> 00:22:34.414
another Palestinian journalist,

00:22:34.726 --> 00:22:38.043
was killed by an Israeli sniper's bullet

00:22:38.465 --> 00:22:41.449
that targeted him
while covering the return marches

00:22:41.785 --> 00:22:45.248
at the Gaza Strip border in 2018

00:22:45.834 --> 00:22:48.616
Israel adopted the same legal argument,

00:22:48.726 --> 00:22:53.038
considering Murtaja's presence
in a military zone

00:22:53.337 --> 00:22:56.849
Allah is the Greatest

00:23:14.589 --> 00:23:16.932
The Israeli Defense Minister at the time,

00:23:17.167 --> 00:23:18.237
Avigdor Lieberman,

00:23:18.385 --> 00:23:19.651
accused Murtaja, the journalist,

00:23:19.760 --> 00:23:22.498
of flying a filming drone
over the occupation soldiers

00:23:52.088 --> 00:23:53.953
The response to Lieberman's accusations

00:23:54.227 --> 00:23:56.125
came from the US State Department,

00:23:56.297 --> 00:23:59.880
which defended US funding
for the media company

00:24:00.209 --> 00:24:02.627
founded by Yasser Murtaja in Gaza

00:24:02.776 --> 00:24:03.378
by saying

00:24:03.682 --> 00:24:07.390
that Murtaja had been vetted under 
U.S. government guidelines

00:24:08.670 --> 00:24:11.325
Despite the refutation
of the Israeli story,

00:24:11.560 --> 00:24:14.958
the Israeli occupation army has not
condemned any of its soldiers

00:24:15.068 --> 00:24:15.755
until today

00:24:19.467 --> 00:24:23.862
We tried to find out
about the soldier who killed Yasser

00:24:24.183 --> 00:24:28.157
by filing a lawsuit
through the Israeli court,

00:24:28.470 --> 00:24:31.077
but the Israeli court did not respond

00:24:31.297 --> 00:24:35.991
It declined to respond to this issue,

00:24:36.241 --> 00:24:39.168
it was not clear who was
the person who killed Yasser

00:24:39.195 --> 00:24:41.629
or who gave the order to kill Yasser

00:24:41.973 --> 00:24:46.816
We found that
the Israeli occupation authorities

00:24:47.261 --> 00:24:49.121
enacted this law

00:24:49.450 --> 00:24:51.184
and not only enacted the law

00:24:51.278 --> 00:24:53.356
but also enacted another law

00:24:53.575 --> 00:24:56.854
that forbids revealing the identity

00:24:57.026 --> 00:25:00.178
of any of the soldiers who fought

00:25:00.232 --> 00:25:02.323
or the Israeli forces who shot

00:25:02.394 --> 00:25:04.435
or caused damage

00:25:04.528 --> 00:25:07.356
or who killed Palestinians

00:25:07.881 --> 00:25:12.415
Thus, it committed two violations

00:25:12.548 --> 00:25:15.459
of Palestinian rights:

00:25:15.677 --> 00:25:19.402
First, it absolved itself
of responsibility as a state,

00:25:19.480 --> 00:25:20.558
as a system, and as an entity

00:25:20.831 --> 00:25:23.938
Secondly, it covered up

00:25:24.125 --> 00:25:26.782
the soldier or the security officer

00:25:26.860 --> 00:25:28.557
who shot fire

00:25:29.614 --> 00:25:31.591
While exploring the Israeli documents,

00:25:31.795 --> 00:25:32.974
we find that Israel

00:25:33.036 --> 00:25:34.704
has amended its military policies

00:25:34.845 --> 00:25:36.290
with the second intifada

00:25:36.509 --> 00:25:38.501
that broke out in 2000

00:25:38.712 --> 00:25:39.929
Accordingly,

00:25:40.312 --> 00:25:42.976
army soldiers and officers
are exempted from accountability

00:25:43.234 --> 00:25:46.450
in case of what it calls
"military activity"

00:25:46.763 --> 00:25:49.676
The most dangerous of all

00:25:50.192 --> 00:25:55.182
is that the Public Prosecutor's Office

00:25:55.495 --> 00:25:57.712
has never investigated

00:25:58.352 --> 00:26:02.318
a case as the investigation should be,

00:26:02.615 --> 00:26:06.473
meaning that there is, for example, a crime

00:26:06.637 --> 00:26:07.778
that occurred,

00:26:08.092 --> 00:26:11.025
as it was done against the martyr Murtaja

00:26:11.556 --> 00:26:13.888
The press jacket was visible on him,

00:26:13.985 --> 00:26:15.510
and the PRESS word

00:26:15.627 --> 00:26:18.853
the camera in his hand

00:26:19.197 --> 00:26:24.305
They could see him clearly,

00:26:24.602 --> 00:26:27.488
yet he was targeted by a sniper

00:26:27.730 --> 00:26:29.136
and killed

00:26:29.691 --> 00:26:33.771
they do not investigate

00:26:33.989 --> 00:26:35.363
this matter

00:26:35.434 --> 00:26:39.084
but instead investigate
whether Israel is at war or not

00:26:39.481 --> 00:26:42.170
Is Israel in a state of conflict or not?

00:26:43.520 --> 00:26:46.685
Therefore, simply opening an investigation

00:26:47.245 --> 00:26:49.088
in the presence of a war crime

00:26:49.167 --> 00:26:49.979
does not occur

00:26:50.260 --> 00:26:53.520
Thus, the Military Prosecutor

00:26:53.582 --> 00:26:56.342
is working to cover up

00:26:58.715 --> 00:26:59.842
this crime

00:27:00.114 --> 00:27:02.825
and give it legal cover from the beginning

00:27:03.059 --> 00:27:05.502
The area where we were filming,

00:27:05.760 --> 00:27:06.580
as you can see,

00:27:06.669 --> 00:27:09.643
was only about 50 metres
away from Salah al-Din

00:27:10.029 --> 00:27:12.529
Salah al-Din is the mainline
for the Gaza Strip,

00:27:13.022 --> 00:27:15.835
so we are in a civilian area
and a populated place

00:27:16.022 --> 00:27:18.089
I remember there were people here watching,

00:27:18.386 --> 00:27:19.166
and there were children

00:27:19.191 --> 00:27:19.738
too

00:27:19.887 --> 00:27:21.292
Pupils were on their way home from school

00:27:21.404 --> 00:27:22.882
We didn't hear any gunfire

00:27:23.296 --> 00:27:24.191
We didn't hear…

00:27:24.332 --> 00:27:26.616
I mean, we didn't hear gunfire
from another side

00:27:26.739 --> 00:27:28.965
We didn't hear things

00:27:29.137 --> 00:27:30.286
that caught our attention

00:27:30.435 --> 00:27:31.523
that made us

00:27:31.562 --> 00:27:33.484
at least take heed

00:27:33.616 --> 00:27:34.702
The shooting that took place

00:27:34.882 --> 00:27:38.523
and led to deaths and injuries
simultaneously,

00:27:38.710 --> 00:27:40.717
I do not think that it is from
the capabilities of the Gaza Strip,

00:27:40.826 --> 00:27:43.438
but it was the enormous tank here

00:27:48.459 --> 00:27:49.977
The killing of journalist Yasser Murtaja

00:27:50.004 --> 00:27:52.445
was utterly premeditated

00:27:52.750 --> 00:27:54.101
He was wearing protective armour,

00:27:54.151 --> 00:27:56.792
and as you know,
it covers the belly area until here,

00:27:57.072 --> 00:27:59.603
and then it is all

00:27:59.728 --> 00:28:01.369
visible from the top,
in addition to the helmet

00:28:01.576 --> 00:28:02.943
So now you are talking about a bullet

00:28:03.115 --> 00:28:04.123
from a professional sniper,

00:28:04.154 --> 00:28:05.248
not any person

00:28:05.287 --> 00:28:06.654
to say that

00:28:06.724 --> 00:28:08.240
the shot was random

00:28:08.318 --> 00:28:09.435
The bullet hit directly
from under the armour

00:28:09.763 --> 00:28:12.070
and penetrated Yasser's abdomen

00:28:17.684 --> 00:28:20.934
Israel classifies the Gaza Strip
as a hostile zone,

00:28:21.254 --> 00:28:24.921
exposing everyone in it
as a military target

00:28:25.468 --> 00:28:28.574
The Israeli judiciary shields
behind this argument

00:28:28.792 --> 00:28:31.657
for not summoning witnesses
and hearing their statements

00:28:31.780 --> 00:28:34.976
in the cases of journalists
who died in Gaza

00:28:35.632 --> 00:28:37.445
Everyone from the Gaza Strip

00:28:38.562 --> 00:28:39.913
since 2001

00:28:39.984 --> 00:28:41.842
cannot go to

00:28:42.154 --> 00:28:45.981
the Israeli military courts,

00:28:46.837 --> 00:28:49.844
and the Israeli judicial system

00:28:50.141 --> 00:28:53.625
has prevented the submission
of these complaints

00:28:53.680 --> 00:28:54.719
when it considered

00:28:54.976 --> 00:28:58.412
the Gaza Strip as hostile territory

00:28:58.936 --> 00:29:01.788
Unfortunately, the Israeli judiciary

00:29:02.194 --> 00:29:05.443
forms along with the general prosecution

00:29:05.707 --> 00:29:08.020
the political and legal cover

00:29:08.426 --> 00:29:12.090
for the war crimes
and crimes against humanity

00:29:12.285 --> 00:29:13.295
committed by the occupation,

00:29:13.365 --> 00:29:16.373
including journalists

00:29:16.513 --> 00:29:19.295
Both local and international

00:29:21.277 --> 00:29:22.675
In the West Bank,

00:29:22.847 --> 00:29:26.410
the pretexts and excuses
for killing journalists have changed,

00:29:26.714 --> 00:29:28.384
but the result is the same

00:29:28.751 --> 00:29:33.318
Another Palestinian journalist
killed in front of the cameras

00:29:46.255 --> 00:29:47.435
Nazih Darwazeh

00:29:47.599 --> 00:29:50.662
He was killed by an Israeli soldier
during his field coverage

00:29:50.771 --> 00:29:53.131
in the city of Nablus in the West Bank

00:29:53.605 --> 00:29:55.839
Today, after 20 years,

00:29:55.988 --> 00:29:57.691
his legal file has been closed,

00:29:57.894 --> 00:30:00.771
and its documents have disappeared
from the Israeli courts

00:30:01.068 --> 00:30:02.646
We interviewed his son, Sameh,

00:30:02.810 --> 00:30:04.982
who was a child
when his father was martyred,

00:30:05.662 --> 00:30:07.176
and today he is striving

00:30:07.333 --> 00:30:10.700
to access his father's file
in the Israeli courts,

00:30:11.068 --> 00:30:13.426
as he reveals being subjected
to financial blackmail,

00:30:13.451 --> 00:30:14.486
as he described it,

00:30:14.590 --> 00:30:16.244
to obtain the file

00:30:17.278 --> 00:30:20.467
Sameh, it is very difficult, difficult,
you must do something

00:30:21.467 --> 00:30:24.006
I started working on the file,

00:30:24.037 --> 00:30:26.732
and by God, seriously, I started

00:30:29.778 --> 00:30:33.340
I am working on it
and I want to win the case

00:30:34.487 --> 00:30:36.682
and I will do the impossible for it

00:30:37.080 --> 00:30:39.536
I am working on it, analysing,
and submitting requests,

00:30:39.614 --> 00:30:43.013
and there are many other requests
that we must submit

00:30:43.412 --> 00:30:47.060
so that we can file the case properly

00:30:47.472 --> 00:30:51.847
Because what they did to you was not fair

00:30:51.951 --> 00:30:54.422
Now you must do what needs to be done

00:30:54.703 --> 00:30:56.836
Sameh, do what needs to be done,
I do not care

00:30:57.047 --> 00:30:59.758
Until Sunday you have to arrange
a sum of money

00:31:00.226 --> 00:31:01.662
You have to get the money ready first

00:31:01.849 --> 00:31:03.170
to proceed

00:31:04.778 --> 00:31:05.887
you can divide them into two instalments

00:31:06.350 --> 00:31:07.905
I want 5000 Jordanian dinars

00:31:08.810 --> 00:31:13.070
These papers are tightly secured

00:31:13.140 --> 00:31:15.741
and I know how to get them out, okay?

00:31:16.022 --> 00:31:18.350
Now I want to tell you something

00:31:18.647 --> 00:31:20.140
if you want because

00:31:20.874 --> 00:31:21.688
I want to go on

00:31:21.818 --> 00:31:23.844
and I tell you that I will continue
and I will not stop

00:31:23.930 --> 00:31:26.289
because I really want these files

00:31:26.391 --> 00:31:28.670
Now

00:31:29.920 --> 00:31:32.748
You are now obliged to pay me

00:31:33.037 --> 00:31:35.709
No documents were sent to us

00:31:35.881 --> 00:31:37.248
by the investigation party

00:31:37.310 --> 00:31:38.850
or any other party

00:31:39.029 --> 00:31:41.490
We tried to look at the papers

00:31:41.740 --> 00:31:42.959
in court

00:31:43.006 --> 00:31:44.929
Still, so far,

00:31:45.288 --> 00:31:46.930
we have not been able to obtain
either the investigation,

00:31:47.000 --> 00:31:49.584
the files inside the court,

00:31:49.946 --> 00:31:51.485
or the soldier's testimony

00:31:51.510 --> 00:31:52.938
if his testimony has already been taken

00:31:53.164 --> 00:31:55.910
Or the force that stormed in that period

00:31:56.213 --> 00:31:58.352
Sometime after my father's martyrdom,

00:31:58.377 --> 00:32:00.846
my mother personally

00:32:00.871 --> 00:32:02.857
appointed a lawyer
from the Arab citizens of Israel,

00:32:03.297 --> 00:32:05.336
and this lawyer

00:32:05.625 --> 00:32:07.055
took her signature on papers

00:32:07.140 --> 00:32:08.703
written in Hebrew,

00:32:08.773 --> 00:32:10.008
the power of attorney and other stuff

00:32:10.217 --> 00:32:12.835
until approximately

00:32:12.943 --> 00:32:14.466
5-6 years passed

00:32:14.599 --> 00:32:15.438
since he was appointed,

00:32:15.563 --> 00:32:16.446
The witnesses

00:32:16.564 --> 00:32:18.993
whose names are known
as we gave him their names

00:32:19.321 --> 00:32:20.779
and contacted the witnesses,

00:32:20.810 --> 00:32:22.163
none of the witnesses

00:32:22.188 --> 00:32:24.265
received a request to attend

00:32:24.554 --> 00:32:25.804
The lawyer had informed the court

00:32:26.125 --> 00:32:27.492
that the witnesses could not attend

00:32:27.517 --> 00:32:28.818
because they were missing
for security reasons,

00:32:29.164 --> 00:32:30.645
meaning they could not obtain permits

00:32:50.861 --> 00:32:52.004
We were standing here,

00:32:52.176 --> 00:32:54.605
and this was just the space
we were hiding in

00:32:54.724 --> 00:32:56.590
We hide from the bullets of the occupation

00:32:56.754 --> 00:32:57.840
Nazih was here,

00:32:57.894 --> 00:32:58.590
and I was next to him

00:32:58.771 --> 00:32:59.920
My shoulder was next to his shoulder

00:33:00.302 --> 00:33:02.108
This was the only space,

00:33:02.350 --> 00:33:03.286
and when the shooting happens,

00:33:03.317 --> 00:33:05.497
we go back inside the house
to protect ourselves a bit

00:33:05.693 --> 00:33:07.091
But eventually, you have to go out
to take pictures

00:33:11.672 --> 00:33:13.961
I heard from his family

00:33:13.986 --> 00:33:15.875
and people about the court,

00:33:16.219 --> 00:33:18.281
but I was not summoned

00:33:18.313 --> 00:33:19.422
and was not asked to attend,

00:33:19.461 --> 00:33:21.365
even though I was close to him
shoulder to shoulder

00:33:21.390 --> 00:33:23.789
I was the best to speak on this subject,

00:33:23.814 --> 00:33:25.031
but I was not summoned,

00:33:25.070 --> 00:33:26.482
and no testimony was taken from me

00:33:26.545 --> 00:33:27.504
Although I was demanding

00:33:27.566 --> 00:33:28.785
and speaking to the media

00:33:29.043 --> 00:33:30.496
that an investigation was necessary

00:33:30.521 --> 00:33:31.293
and that I was ready

00:33:31.504 --> 00:33:32.933
I am also fluent in Hebrew and English,

00:33:32.965 --> 00:33:34.183
and I am ready to speak all languages,

00:33:34.208 --> 00:33:35.474
but no one contacted me,

00:33:35.545 --> 00:33:37.451
and no one came to inquire
about what happened

00:33:37.569 --> 00:33:38.412
I wish I had been summoned

00:33:38.506 --> 00:33:39.928
but if they didn't give me a permit

00:33:39.953 --> 00:33:41.451
I wouldn't be able to go
It would be the same outcome

00:33:41.733 --> 00:33:44.603
So, if one of the colleagues were summoned

00:33:44.783 --> 00:33:46.072
and did not go
because he did not obtain a permit,

00:33:46.111 --> 00:33:47.775
the result would have been the same

00:33:48.002 --> 00:33:49.408
Even if I was summoned

00:33:49.474 --> 00:33:50.865
yet banned from going

00:33:51.070 --> 00:33:52.500
it would be the same idea

00:33:52.646 --> 00:33:53.992
Whether any colleague

00:33:54.024 --> 00:33:55.251
was contacted to attend,

00:33:55.498 --> 00:33:56.631
or wasn't,

00:33:56.735 --> 00:33:58.953
all is the same
because everyone will not reach

00:33:59.328 --> 00:33:59.814
the court

00:33:59.814 --> 00:34:02.575
I wished to reach the court and speak

00:34:02.700 --> 00:34:06.927
fluently about what happened because I am an eyewitness
I was right next to Nazih Darwazeh

00:34:07.177 --> 00:34:09.029
when he was targeted and killed
in cold blood,

00:34:09.084 --> 00:34:10.670
but this is what happened

00:34:12.078 --> 00:34:14.820
We contacted the American Associated Press

00:34:15.289 --> 00:34:18.408
to inquire about developments
in the case of Nazih Darwazeh,

00:34:18.510 --> 00:34:20.635
who was a cameraman for the agency

00:34:20.893 --> 00:34:23.393
However, despite many correspondences
and attempts,

00:34:23.799 --> 00:34:25.659
we did not receive any response from them

00:34:25.895 --> 00:34:27.863
until the date of
broadcasting this investigation

00:34:28.106 --> 00:34:29.903
In fact,

00:34:30.121 --> 00:34:31.305
the AP agency

00:34:31.357 --> 00:34:32.404
visited us

00:34:32.459 --> 00:34:34.928
after the assassination

00:34:35.373 --> 00:34:37.342
and attended the funeral,

00:34:38.467 --> 00:34:41.287
but the problem is that
they did not take any legal action

00:34:41.645 --> 00:34:42.950
They did not follow up on any file

00:34:43.161 --> 00:34:44.404
legally,

00:34:44.654 --> 00:34:46.317
although it is a well-known agency

00:34:46.356 --> 00:34:47.934
and is supposed to take it upon itself

00:34:47.997 --> 00:34:48.897
to research this issue

00:34:49.209 --> 00:34:50.584
No legal effort

00:34:50.709 --> 00:34:52.967
was made in this matter

00:34:53.342 --> 00:34:54.990
and the case was not pursued,

00:34:55.186 --> 00:34:57.385
neither in Israeli courts

00:34:57.416 --> 00:34:58.961
nor in international courts

00:34:59.352 --> 00:35:02.242
I think that the AP

00:35:02.320 --> 00:35:04.864
is an American agency,

00:35:05.598 --> 00:35:07.551
so it is possible

00:35:07.598 --> 00:35:09.285
that they have…

00:35:11.207 --> 00:35:12.511
They did not follow up on this matter

00:35:12.566 --> 00:35:15.254
because it is possible

00:35:15.394 --> 00:35:16.840
since they are based in America,

00:35:16.896 --> 00:35:19.151
this may pose

00:35:19.495 --> 00:35:21.768
a problem for them

00:35:21.964 --> 00:35:23.128
in their work

00:35:24.706 --> 00:35:25.888
This document issued

00:35:25.913 --> 00:35:28.529
by the Israeli court in Haifa

00:35:28.919 --> 00:35:30.474
related to the case

00:35:30.499 --> 00:35:32.239
of the assassination of journalist
Nazih Darwazeh

00:35:32.442 --> 00:35:34.099
reveals that the closure of the case

00:35:34.153 --> 00:35:37.300
resulted from the witnesses
not appearing before the court

00:35:37.675 --> 00:35:38.552
This pretext

00:35:38.584 --> 00:35:40.224
was repeated in more than one case,

00:35:40.741 --> 00:35:43.132
given the deliberate prevention
of witnesses

00:35:43.413 --> 00:35:44.871
from accessing the courts

00:35:44.896 --> 00:35:46.701
by the Israeli authorities

00:35:47.295 --> 00:35:49.209
I remember that the witnesses

00:35:49.271 --> 00:35:51.474
who were present
and whose names we have submitted

00:35:51.638 --> 00:35:52.654
did not attend any hearings

00:35:52.701 --> 00:35:54.125
and were not even notified of

00:35:54.430 --> 00:35:55.352
the dates of the hearings

00:35:55.563 --> 00:35:56.415
to attend

00:35:56.813 --> 00:35:59.836
None of our testimonies was heard

00:36:00.290 --> 00:36:02.542
in court because initially,
we were not informed

00:36:02.597 --> 00:36:03.667
of any session or any date,

00:36:04.123 --> 00:36:06.087
meaning that

00:36:06.538 --> 00:36:08.382
we felt that there was collusion

00:36:08.407 --> 00:36:09.741
between the court

00:36:09.773 --> 00:36:12.000
and the assigned lawyer

00:36:12.374 --> 00:36:14.334
Because, actually

00:36:14.740 --> 00:36:16.764
I learned in those days, from the lawyer

00:36:16.826 --> 00:36:19.537
that an internal investigation
had been carried out in the army

00:36:20.115 --> 00:36:22.334
And that investigation

00:36:23.732 --> 00:36:25.310
resulted in

00:36:25.335 --> 00:36:28.295
concealing the name of the soldier
who carried out the assassination,

00:36:28.752 --> 00:36:30.692
and then

00:36:30.755 --> 00:36:32.247
the information disappeared utterly

00:36:32.293 --> 00:36:34.611
The occupation does not want
to prosecute any soldier,

00:36:34.636 --> 00:36:35.697
whether in the past, present or future

00:36:36.176 --> 00:36:37.780
The occupying state

00:36:38.108 --> 00:36:39.428
the most significant thing it can do

00:36:39.491 --> 00:36:41.246
even if convicted is paying money

00:36:41.360 --> 00:36:43.384
Many cases have ended in compensation

00:36:43.665 --> 00:36:45.720
They say we are not
prosecuting our soldiers

00:36:45.759 --> 00:36:46.890
Our soldiers were at war

00:36:47.162 --> 00:36:49.099
And I heard this matter in court,

00:36:49.175 --> 00:36:50.584
as I was present in other sessions

00:36:50.936 --> 00:36:51.975
that this is war

00:36:52.459 --> 00:36:53.872
You are present in this war

00:36:53.912 --> 00:36:55.053
and satisfied for yourself what will be
You came to battle

00:36:55.263 --> 00:36:57.045
As a journalist,
you bear your responsibility

00:36:57.286 --> 00:36:58.905
and are part of this war

00:36:58.975 --> 00:37:00.374
If you die, we are not responsible

00:37:00.944 --> 00:37:02.772
Suppose the party
conducting the investigation

00:37:02.819 --> 00:37:04.079
is affiliated with

00:37:04.157 --> 00:37:05.603
the Israeli army,

00:37:05.638 --> 00:37:07.227
one of the arms of the Israeli military

00:37:07.852 --> 00:37:08.907
In that case, it will naturally

00:37:09.334 --> 00:37:10.766
investigate the file

00:37:10.881 --> 00:37:11.727
in a way

00:37:12.412 --> 00:37:14.413
that protects

00:37:14.811 --> 00:37:15.710
its story

00:37:15.827 --> 00:37:17.382
Even if we go to

00:37:17.429 --> 00:37:18.382
the judicial system,

00:37:18.624 --> 00:37:20.311
assuming the Israeli judicial system

00:37:20.710 --> 00:37:22.740
The Israeli judicial system

00:37:22.999 --> 00:37:24.186
deals with the same mentality

00:37:24.413 --> 00:37:26.014
It is shameful and humiliating

00:37:26.874 --> 00:37:28.663
for any judicial body

00:37:30.528 --> 00:37:31.677
to constitute

00:37:32.709 --> 00:37:34.067
a legal framework

00:37:35.005 --> 00:37:36.825
for war crimes

00:37:36.856 --> 00:37:38.739
and crimes against humanity,

00:37:39.287 --> 00:37:41.919
mainly if it targets

00:37:42.599 --> 00:37:43.666
civilians

00:37:43.742 --> 00:37:44.773
and specifically if

00:37:45.201 --> 00:37:47.288
it targets freedom of opinion
and expression

00:37:48.695 --> 00:37:50.796
In front of all this
evidence and accusations

00:37:50.828 --> 00:37:52.625
against the Israeli occupation,

00:37:53.360 --> 00:37:55.399
we sent a letter to the Israeli army

00:37:55.911 --> 00:37:59.192
to ask about the issues of journalists
raised in this investigation

00:37:59.724 --> 00:38:02.633
and the allegations levelled against it
of destroying evidence,

00:38:02.942 --> 00:38:04.695
covering up the killer soldiers

00:38:05.021 --> 00:38:06.695
and facilitating their impunity

00:38:07.452 --> 00:38:10.976
We received a lengthy response from
the spokesperson of the occupation army

00:38:11.451 --> 00:38:12.638
He avoided mentioning

00:38:12.701 --> 00:38:14.865
any of the names of the victim journalists

00:38:15.287 --> 00:38:16.710
and the details of their files

00:38:17.273 --> 00:38:19.492
He repeatedly elaborated
on the security pretexts

00:38:19.835 --> 00:38:22.235
and talked about activities
of a combative nature,

00:38:22.260 --> 00:38:23.259
as he described,

00:38:23.607 --> 00:38:25.720
in the places where the victims fall,

00:38:26.044 --> 00:38:27.052
including journalists

00:38:29.373 --> 00:38:31.936
Israel's systematic policy of denial

00:38:31.975 --> 00:38:34.075
and evasion of accountability
and responsibility

00:38:34.623 --> 00:38:37.305
was apparent in cases
of targeting journalists,

00:38:37.873 --> 00:38:40.422
the latest of which was the case of
colleague Shireen Abu Akleh

00:38:40.904 --> 00:38:42.508
According to private sources,

00:38:42.723 --> 00:38:44.812
a senior Israeli official

00:38:44.837 --> 00:38:47.789
in the office of former Defense Minister
Benny Gantz

00:38:48.230 --> 00:38:50.237
admitted to US officials

00:38:50.605 --> 00:38:51.605
that Shireen

00:38:51.966 --> 00:38:54.935
was killed by gunfire fired
by Israeli soldiers by mistake

00:38:55.434 --> 00:38:56.458
Still, Israel

00:38:56.896 --> 00:38:59.170
will not announce it
or officially recognize it

00:39:00.865 --> 00:39:02.406
In light of an international campaign

00:39:02.431 --> 00:39:04.667
condemning the assassination of Shireen Abu Akleh,

00:39:05.028 --> 00:39:07.214
Al Jazeera Media Network

00:39:07.505 --> 00:39:10.285
filed a case with the
International Criminal Court in The Hague

00:39:11.183 --> 00:39:12.105
Al Jazeera announced

00:39:12.552 --> 00:39:13.745
that this step

00:39:14.068 --> 00:39:16.734
came after its legal team
conducted an investigation

00:39:16.759 --> 00:39:18.218
that revealed new evidence

00:39:18.765 --> 00:39:19.750
that clearly showed

00:39:20.101 --> 00:39:23.701
that Shireen and her colleagues
were exposed to direct gunfire

00:39:23.724 --> 00:39:25.425
by the Israeli occupation army

00:39:26.027 --> 00:39:29.590
And the claim by the Israeli authorities
that they mistakenly killed Shireen

00:39:30.144 --> 00:39:31.855
during an exchange of fire

00:39:32.308 --> 00:39:33.722
is baseless.

00:39:34.552 --> 00:39:35.685
Concurrently,

00:39:36.068 --> 00:39:38.489
the Palestinian Journalists Syndicate,

00:39:38.514 --> 00:39:40.839
in cooperation with the
International Federation of Journalists,

00:39:41.396 --> 00:39:44.799
filed a complaint with the Office of the
Attorney General of the International Criminal Court

00:39:45.388 --> 00:39:48.404
In addition to Shireen Abu Akleh's file,
the complaint included

00:39:49.005 --> 00:39:52.166
the two files of the assassination of
journalists Yasser Murtaja

00:39:52.463 --> 00:39:53.922
and Ahmed Abu Hussein in Gaza

00:39:54.345 --> 00:39:55.438
And also the two files

00:39:55.470 --> 00:39:57.462
of the injuries of the two journalists,
Moath Amarneh

00:39:57.849 --> 00:39:59.634
and Nidal Shtayyeh in the West Bank

00:40:00.075 --> 00:40:02.066
Exactly on September 20,

00:40:02.622 --> 00:40:05.051
we submitted the file to the
International Criminal Court

00:40:05.113 --> 00:40:07.309
We were subjected to logistical harassment,

00:40:07.731 --> 00:40:09.145
but ultimately,

00:40:09.207 --> 00:40:11.950
the International Federation
and we handed over the file

00:40:12.013 --> 00:40:14.029
So we had an international
cover and umbrella

00:40:14.285 --> 00:40:16.332
for our international movement

00:40:16.902 --> 00:40:19.129
We handed over this file,

00:40:19.183 --> 00:40:21.480
and Tony Abu Akleh, the brother of
the martyr Shireen, was with us

00:40:21.886 --> 00:40:24.043
Al-Jazeera was thankful

00:40:24.082 --> 00:40:25.754
that it covered

00:40:25.808 --> 00:40:26.481
the matter

00:40:28.349 --> 00:40:30.544
On September 6, we received a letter

00:40:30.575 --> 00:40:32.146
that I will give to you

00:40:32.614 --> 00:40:36.614
It includes what it means
to have started the procedures,

00:40:37.145 --> 00:40:40.035
but we consider that insufficient

00:40:40.613 --> 00:40:44.717
This is the response that the
Palestinian Journalists Syndicate received

00:40:44.740 --> 00:40:46.365
from the International Criminal Court

00:40:46.390 --> 00:40:48.086
after submitting the complaint,

00:40:48.133 --> 00:40:49.984
informing it of receiving the application

00:40:50.289 --> 00:40:51.664
and proceeding to review it

00:40:52.695 --> 00:40:54.125
Remarkably,

00:40:54.150 --> 00:40:55.899
the approach to the
International Criminal Court

00:40:56.234 --> 00:40:58.820
was limited to cases targeting journalists

00:40:59.289 --> 00:41:01.589
that occurred after 2014

00:41:02.253 --> 00:41:04.174
This raised several questions

00:41:04.498 --> 00:41:08.182
about the fate of the targeting of
journalists in the preceding years

00:41:08.685 --> 00:41:10.216
A clear and explicit statement

00:41:10.502 --> 00:41:11.713
in the Rome Charter

00:41:12.232 --> 00:41:13.897
of the International Criminal Court

00:41:14.607 --> 00:41:16.904
states in

00:41:17.458 --> 00:41:18.958
a simple, clear,

00:41:19.771 --> 00:41:21.021
and categoric that

00:41:21.574 --> 00:41:23.605
the International Criminal Court

00:41:23.645 --> 00:41:26.004
does not consider cases retrospectively

00:41:26.550 --> 00:41:29.893
In the sense that the state,
since the ratification

00:41:31.341 --> 00:41:33.261
and signing of the Rome Charter,

00:41:33.449 --> 00:41:36.644
only issues related to it

00:41:37.168 --> 00:41:38.125
are considered,

00:41:38.357 --> 00:41:42.295
and claims before that are not considered

00:41:42.475 --> 00:41:44.952
Of course, we thought of going to
the International Criminal Court

00:41:45.498 --> 00:41:48.686
and it was obligatory to go to do so;
however,

00:41:49.085 --> 00:41:51.350
but unfortunately,
no one cared about the issue,

00:41:51.655 --> 00:41:53.499
and no one offered a helping hand

00:41:53.561 --> 00:41:55.555
No one has asked for a single document yet

00:41:55.919 --> 00:42:00.156
Unfortunately, the Journalists Syndicate
has not yet asked us

00:42:00.622 --> 00:42:02.716
for a single document
on the subject,

00:42:03.145 --> 00:42:04.953
despite their knowledge that the file
has been closed more than once

00:42:05.122 --> 00:42:06.937
We are prosecuting the occupation based on

00:42:06.977 --> 00:42:10.203
the crime committed
against Palestinian journalists

00:42:10.633 --> 00:42:13.526
Also, what is the fate of those
whose names we did not raise, for example

00:42:13.551 --> 00:42:15.151
Nazih Darwazeh, for instance,

00:42:15.261 --> 00:42:17.385
was before 2014, as we mentioned earlier

00:42:17.791 --> 00:42:18.526
Fadel Shana

00:42:19.020 --> 00:42:21.643
Between 2014 and 2023,

00:42:21.685 --> 00:42:23.533
people whose names have not been included

00:42:23.838 --> 00:42:25.021
But the principle

00:42:25.080 --> 00:42:26.994
on which we want to prosecute them

00:42:27.026 --> 00:42:29.768
is the principle of crimes against
Palestinian journalists,

00:42:30.001 --> 00:42:33.021
and international law describes them

00:42:33.060 --> 00:42:34.766
as war crimes

00:42:35.149 --> 00:42:37.985
Now, almost a year has passed since
the assassination of Shireen

00:42:38.477 --> 00:42:40.470
What did the International Criminal Court do?

00:42:40.821 --> 00:42:42.736
We notice that there is
delay and sluggishness,

00:42:43.175 --> 00:42:46.261
we want to know if the reason is political,

00:42:46.682 --> 00:42:48.261
but we should put pressure

00:42:48.542 --> 00:42:52.623
Obviously, the International Criminal
Court Prosecutor,

00:42:53.409 --> 00:42:56.284
Mr Karim Khan or Mr KK,

00:42:56.653 --> 00:42:59.044
since he took over this

00:42:59.076 --> 00:43:01.669
about two years ago

00:43:01.694 --> 00:43:04.802
and became the ICC Prosecutor.

00:43:06.972 --> 00:43:09.309
Clearly, he fully practices politicization

00:43:09.341 --> 00:43:10.817
and selectivity

00:43:11.334 --> 00:43:14.504
when dealing with the Palestinian file

00:43:15.076 --> 00:43:17.160
I mean, 

00:43:17.684 --> 00:43:19.973
he activated the Ukraine file,

00:43:20.903 --> 00:43:22.996
and caused a lot of fuss

00:43:23.020 --> 00:43:24.317
Within one year,

00:43:25.138 --> 00:43:27.504
an arrest warrant

00:43:28.216 --> 00:43:29.223
had been issued

00:43:30.315 --> 00:43:31.622
against Putin,

00:43:32.310 --> 00:43:33.887
and dozens

00:43:35.068 --> 00:43:37.357
of sanctions had been issued

00:43:37.825 --> 00:43:39.606
against the Russian Federation,

00:43:40.067 --> 00:43:41.934
six waves

00:43:42.653 --> 00:43:45.059
of successive sanctions.

00:43:45.559 --> 00:43:47.309
Yet, on the Palestinian issue,

00:43:47.801 --> 00:43:50.649
he did not move a single millimetre,

00:43:50.821 --> 00:43:53.500
even at the level of
contact and communication

00:43:53.938 --> 00:43:56.235
with lawyers or with the victims

00:43:56.313 --> 00:43:58.610
or visiting areas

00:43:58.915 --> 00:44:00.688
Or even give a single statement

00:44:01.060 --> 00:44:03.688
about what is happening in the
occupied territories of war crimes

00:44:04.118 --> 00:44:05.835
and crimes against humanity

00:44:06.472 --> 00:44:09.787
We contacted the Office of the Prosecutor
of the International Criminal Court,

00:44:09.810 --> 00:44:10.578
Karim Khan,

00:44:10.860 --> 00:44:12.359
for an interview about

00:44:12.398 --> 00:44:14.570
the developments of the submitted complaint

00:44:15.047 --> 00:44:17.805
and the fate of the cases of
targeting Palestinian journalists

00:44:18.344 --> 00:44:20.707
by the Israeli occupation army

00:44:20.871 --> 00:44:23.293
We received a response
that the Public Prosecutor

00:44:23.473 --> 00:44:25.723
will not be able to conduct this interview

00:44:26.176 --> 00:44:27.387
I fear

00:44:28.153 --> 00:44:29.809
that one day

00:44:31.348 --> 00:44:32.795
there will be pressure
from the politicians,

00:44:33.325 --> 00:44:35.067
and they withdraw the case,

00:44:36.569 --> 00:44:37.513
as happened with other cases

00:44:38.224 --> 00:44:40.130
That is why they keep us

00:44:40.505 --> 00:44:41.513
from details

00:44:42.233 --> 00:44:43.545
of what is happening

00:44:45.326 --> 00:44:46.998
in this case.

00:44:47.247 --> 00:44:49.083
However, Mr Nasser, there is

00:44:49.616 --> 00:44:51.381
a fear on the part of the victims

00:44:51.428 --> 00:44:53.248
or some victims that political pressures

00:44:53.655 --> 00:44:55.373
will affect

00:44:55.405 --> 00:44:56.802
the future and the outcome

00:44:57.178 --> 00:44:58.319
of this legal course

00:44:58.608 --> 00:44:59.505
in the International Criminal Court

00:44:59.530 --> 00:45:00.373
First: We are an independent Syndicate

00:45:00.404 --> 00:45:03.232
representing Palestinian journalists
and their rights

00:45:03.269 --> 00:45:06.761
Then we prepared this for
all the martyrs and the wounded;

00:45:07.373 --> 00:45:08.756
therefore, this cannot happen,

00:45:08.795 --> 00:45:09.826
but we are also

00:45:09.975 --> 00:45:13.577
partners with the
International Federation of Journalists

00:45:13.928 --> 00:45:16.788
Even if pressures were exerted
on the Palestinian Authority?

00:45:16.813 --> 00:45:17.959
This is not our business!

00:45:18.303 --> 00:45:20.405
I believe that the position
of the authority is clear

00:45:20.772 --> 00:45:22.889
I am not a spokesperson for the authority,

00:45:22.928 --> 00:45:26.744
but I tell you clearly that

00:45:26.838 --> 00:45:30.220
the statements of the Palestinian leadership,
headed by President Abu Mazen,

00:45:30.595 --> 00:45:33.159
call for going to
the International Criminal Court,

00:45:33.357 --> 00:45:34.396
and I believe that in recent days

00:45:34.427 --> 00:45:35.503
they have submitted files

00:45:36.441 --> 00:45:38.238
or will submit other files

00:45:38.550 --> 00:45:41.208
against the occupation.
Therefore, this issue of the criminal court

00:45:41.263 --> 00:45:44.232
is a process that has begun
and has not yet stopped

00:45:44.551 --> 00:45:47.685
After Israel evaded many cases
by killing journalists,

00:45:48.060 --> 00:45:48.951
we noticed an approach

00:45:49.498 --> 00:45:52.314
towards the International Criminal Court

00:45:52.339 --> 00:45:53.447
for the sake of justice

00:45:53.927 --> 00:45:55.306
Do you think this road

00:45:55.869 --> 00:45:57.283
will be smooth,

00:45:57.931 --> 00:45:58.724
or will

00:45:59.400 --> 00:46:00.588
Israel also seek

00:46:00.904 --> 00:46:01.601
to evade it,

00:46:01.758 --> 00:46:04.281
and international circumstances
will help it in that?

00:46:04.648 --> 00:46:07.914
I'm not sure if it will work

00:46:08.008 --> 00:46:09.357
But, still, I think

00:46:09.470 --> 00:46:12.509
this should be the next step

00:46:12.665 --> 00:46:15.555
to refer all the murders 

00:46:15.580 --> 00:46:17.773
to the International Criminal Court

00:46:17.883 --> 00:46:19.209
to be reviewed

00:46:19.349 --> 00:46:21.115
because in all the lawsuits

00:46:21.170 --> 00:46:22.615
that I reviewed,

00:46:22.677 --> 00:46:25.061
I still see it looks like

00:46:25.194 --> 00:46:26.826
an unfinished novel

00:46:26.967 --> 00:46:29.028
So, I would like to see the next step

00:46:29.215 --> 00:46:31.598
I would like to see all these lawsuits

00:46:31.630 --> 00:46:33.083
being reinvestigated

00:46:33.200 --> 00:46:36.989
and a final solution
and conclusion reached

00:46:42.551 --> 00:46:44.231
We think about the file every day,

00:46:44.926 --> 00:46:45.426
Fadel

00:46:45.942 --> 00:46:47.239
Fadel's file is a file

00:46:48.543 --> 00:46:49.318
that we, as a family,

00:46:50.959 --> 00:46:51.873
have not forgotten

00:46:52.412 --> 00:46:54.162
The file is still on the table,

00:46:54.795 --> 00:46:56.435
and the file is still open,

00:46:56.974 --> 00:46:58.030
awaiting justice

00:47:03.819 --> 00:47:06.319
As for me, I have no problem

00:47:06.344 --> 00:47:08.608
going to any court in the world

00:47:09.116 --> 00:47:12.171
to prove my father's right to this crime,

00:47:12.593 --> 00:47:14.038
as he was assassinated in cold blood,

00:47:14.390 --> 00:47:15.871
and to protect

00:47:16.999 --> 00:47:19.728
the young journalists in the field

00:47:19.790 --> 00:47:21.243
From the first moment,

00:47:21.435 --> 00:47:24.564
I considered submitting this file

00:47:25.165 --> 00:47:27.798
to the International Criminal Court,
not just today

00:47:28.321 --> 00:47:29.596
However, the inaction

00:47:29.621 --> 00:47:31.354
that occurred in the past period

00:47:31.471 --> 00:47:33.268
prevented us from submitting

00:47:33.612 --> 00:47:35.362
the file to
the International Criminal Court

00:47:35.737 --> 00:47:38.284
because this file was not embraced

00:47:38.693 --> 00:47:39.771
even by the former unions

00:47:39.815 --> 00:47:42.313
and trade union councils

00:47:42.680 --> 00:47:44.477
No one knocked on our door, asking us

00:47:44.684 --> 00:47:46.133
to submit the file legally

00:47:48.099 --> 00:47:49.891
Obstacles through which

00:47:49.934 --> 00:47:51.633
we can

00:47:51.915 --> 00:47:54.290
feel that Yasser's case is not

00:47:54.719 --> 00:47:55.500
ongoing

00:47:55.922 --> 00:47:59.393
It is not justifying the occupation
for sniping,

00:47:59.471 --> 00:48:01.541
targeting, or killing Yasser

00:48:02.260 --> 00:48:03.697
or the journalists after him

00:48:04.151 --> 00:48:06.072
They always try to evade the situation

00:48:06.510 --> 00:48:09.640
and justify the Israeli narrative

00:48:09.731 --> 00:48:12.145
Then he tries to show that you're an abuser

00:48:12.170 --> 00:48:15.576
when you're really only fighting
with your camera

00:48:17.069 --> 00:48:18.959
After the injury,

00:48:19.428 --> 00:48:20.358
my life turned around

00:48:20.850 --> 00:48:22.029
360 degrees

00:48:22.881 --> 00:48:26.059
I became like

00:48:26.084 --> 00:48:29.608
an old man in his 90s

00:48:30.295 --> 00:48:32.524
who only had a few things left

00:48:33.118 --> 00:48:35.617
to do before he died

00:48:36.172 --> 00:48:37.024
Or as a young child

00:48:38.579 --> 00:48:40.039
who would like to live happily

00:48:41.016 --> 00:48:42.297
so that he

00:48:42.633 --> 00:48:45.047
can enjoy life.
I try to forget as much as I can

00:48:48.219 --> 00:48:49.369
what happened to me

00:48:51.229 --> 00:48:53.076
so that I do not live

00:48:53.349 --> 00:48:55.549
with the burden of the bullet in my head

00:48:56.244 --> 00:48:57.682
that could, at any moment,

00:48:59.373 --> 00:48:59.873
move

00:49:00.654 --> 00:49:01.228
or

00:49:02.298 --> 00:49:06.375
cause me major problems

00:49:07.162 --> 00:49:09.915
that make me lose the ability

00:49:11.680 --> 00:49:13.146
to deal with the people around me

00:49:13.177 --> 00:49:14.770
If I can deal with the people around me,
why not?

00:49:15.341 --> 00:49:16.942
I try to enjoy as much as I can

00:49:18.747 --> 00:49:20.529
until Allah chooses something better for us

00:49:33.511 --> 00:49:35.666
In the story of Shireen,

00:49:35.690 --> 00:49:37.230
the martyr and witness,

00:49:37.615 --> 00:49:39.490
and dozens of companions on the path

00:49:39.958 --> 00:49:41.357
who preceded her,

00:49:41.740 --> 00:49:43.638
a test of justice

00:49:44.083 --> 00:49:47.380
in the face of an occupation that is not
satisfied with killing journalists in the field

00:49:48.005 --> 00:49:50.357
but instead seeks to destroy evidence

00:49:50.382 --> 00:49:52.654
and block the way for trials

00:49:52.700 --> 00:49:53.959
and impunity

00:49:54.654 --> 00:49:56.685
in a world of double standards

00:49:57.544 --> 00:49:59.888
and it is only the Tip of the Iceberg

